     3,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hi.<p>On Fri, Mar 2, 2012 at 1:37 AM, hiberbear &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">xshi...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt; Hi everyone:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; I am running aroma.affymetrix on human exon array (HuEx-1_0-st-v2). I find a<br>&gt; confusing thing about the gene summary:<br>&gt; trFit is identical to  ExFit.<br>&gt; My understanding is that if mergeGroups=TRUE, I may get a single value for<br>&gt; each transcript. for every sample,<br>&gt; if mergeGroups=FALSE, I will get the exon value for each transcription for<br>&gt; every sample, and I won&#39;t get a single value for the whole transcipt</p><p>Yes, that is correct.</p><p>&gt;<br>&gt; plmTr &lt;- ExonRmaPlm(csN, mergeGroups=TRUE)<br>&gt; fit(plmTr, verbose=verbose) # this takes a while!<br>&gt; cesTr &lt;- getChipEffectSet(plmTr)<br>&gt; trFit &lt;- extractDataFrame(cesTr, units=NULL, addNames=TRUE<br>&gt;<br>&gt; plmEx &lt;- ExonRmaPlm(csN, mergeGroups=FALSE)<br>&gt; fit(plmEx, verbose=verbose) # this takes a while!<br>&gt; cesEx &lt;- getChipEffectSet(plmEx)<br>&gt; ExFit &lt;- extractDataFrame(cesEx, units=NULL, addNames=TRUE) # this takes a<br>&gt; while!</p><p>I&#39;ve just verified with the latest aroma.affymetrix (v2.4.0), and I<br>cannot reproduce this when I use then<br>HuEx-1_0-st-v2,coreR3,A20071112,EP.cdf CDF file.  Which CDF file are<br>you using?</p><p>/Henrik</p></blockquote>"
